n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: You think so?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'm convinced that's the case.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: I'll take your word for it, Kristi.", "id": 1}, {"time": "", "image": "engenn11le09ob05re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Now that we're done with that, we can schedule a meeting with the illustrator.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: We also need to discuss another matter.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: What's that?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: I'm of the opinion that this typeface has got to be changed.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Personally, I don't see an issue with it. However, since this a children's book, it might be a good idea.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: I'm glad we're on the same page. This typeface is just not that kid-friendly.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I did read somewhere that the typeface for a children's text ought to be a warm, friendly design with simple, large letter shapes. The counters should be rounded and open, not angular or rectangular.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: That makes a lot of sense. Because children are learning to read, the typefaces used should be inviting and easy-to-read.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: To my way of thinking, the text should be larger. Perhaps, somewhere between 20 to 24 point depending on the typeface we choose.", "id": 2}, {"time": "", "image": "engenn11le09ob05re2img03.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: That may be a bit too large, but we can decide on that later. Also, this page here,  I think we should avoid the all caps ... We'll discuss this later. I have to take this call. Since we know what we need to talk about, I suggest you see if you can get the illustrator to come in this afternoon.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Alright. I'm on it.", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le09ob05re2vid01", "coverimg": "engenn11le09ob05re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1}, {"type": "video", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "2000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: Kristi, have you seen these illustrations?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: No, I haven't. How are they?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: As far as I'm concerned, it's just not that aesthetically pleasing.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Hmm, I see what you mean. Because there isn't a balance between the visuals and the white space on the page, it comes off as unappealing.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: I'm convinced it's the contour lines that lack definition; therefore, it's not that noticeable. What I think needs to happen is that these lines need to be darkened.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I disagree. Since there is a lot of white space on the page, they don't pop out. If we reduce the white space, it should be fine.", "id": 1}, {"time": "47500", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: You think so?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'm convinced that's the case.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: I'll take your word for it, Kristi.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Now that we're done with that, we can schedule a meeting with the illustrator.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: We also need to discuss the typeface. I'm of the opinion that this typeface needs to be changed.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Personally, I don't see an issue ... However, since this a children's book, it might be a good idea.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: I'm glad we're on the same page. This typeface needs to be more kid-friendly. I read somewhere that children's text ought to be warm and friendly designs -- simple, with large letter shapes. The contours should be round and open, not angular or rectangular.\n<br/>", "id": 2}, {"time": "96250", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: That makes a lot of sense. Because children are learning to read, the typefaces used should be inviting and easy-to-read.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Denise</span>: To my way of thinking, the text needs to be larger. Perhaps, 20 to 24 point depending on the typeface we choose. And on this page, I think we should avoid all caps. <br/>We'll discuss this further ... I really need to take this call. Since we know what we need to talk about, why don't you contact the illustrator and get him to come in this afternoon?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Alright. I'm on it.", "id": 3}], "video_src": "engenn11le09ob05re2vid01"}}], "id": 2}]}]}